                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b38bc7c1-6055-3d08-869b-3b9c544417b9",
                        "entry_id": "834fc100-c184-3b64-a6a1-565db79bf7ef",
                        "glosses": [
                            "орнитол. самая крупная птица из группы американских грифов, распространенная в Андах"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2dd2472-8410-4686-b08a-44c6acb371c7",
                                "sense_id": "b38bc7c1-6055-3d08-869b-3b9c544417b9",
                                "text": "— Где ты видал таких маленьких кондоров? У кондора размах крыльев достигает трёх метров, а у этого и двух нет. Согласен, голова странноватая. Но во всем остальном орёл."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "137ae527-60bb-3389-ba3e-bae10b57f02e",
                        "entry_id": "834fc100-c184-3b64-a6a1-565db79bf7ef",
                        "glosses": [
                            "нумизм. золотая и серебряная монета, обращавшаяся в некоторых южноамериканских странах (Чили, Колумбия, Эквадор) в период 1851-1933 годов"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "10f4c037-5ec5-48c2-9612-932daeb0bf32",
                        "source_entry_id": "834fc100-c184-3b64-a6a1-565db79bf7ef",
                        "target_lang_word": "condor",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "condor",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "119feb87-19ee-328e-b793-0735a13082e1",
                                        "entry_id": "d7dcc819-1f41-33f1-b55f-e0a268eebb56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Either of two New World vultures, Vultur gryphus of the Andes or Gymnogyps californianus, a nearly extinct vulture of the mountains of California."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64cdf041-e7ba-44cf-b7e7-70bc61ecd7c0",
                                                "sense_id": "119feb87-19ee-328e-b793-0735a13082e1",
                                                "text": "The condor lays a couple of eggs and the ostrich a score, and yet in the same country the condor may be the more numerous of the two: the Fulmar petrel lays but one egg, yet it is believed to be the most numerous bird in the world."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7018d688-4bd8-39a9-9a81-8100b3ab7863",
                                        "entry_id": "d7dcc819-1f41-33f1-b55f-e0a268eebb56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A gold coin of some South American countries bearing the figure of one of these vultures."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "38081db8-7325-38a3-9405-49ae7765781a",
                                        "entry_id": "d7dcc819-1f41-33f1-b55f-e0a268eebb56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An Argentinian short range ballistic missile."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a86a0f3-a718-3c41-a689-45e445be3cff",
                                        "entry_id": "d7dcc819-1f41-33f1-b55f-e0a268eebb56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The completion of a hole four strokes under par (a quadruple birdie, triple eagle, or double albatross)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "68b7177e-d254-3cf3-a204-16b4cba9106e",
                                        "entry_id": "d7dcc819-1f41-33f1-b55f-e0a268eebb56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A combination of four options of the same type at four strike prices, giving limited profit and limited risk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cfcc6689-49b2-4b0c-8b2d-5f3c0ed59180",
                        "source_entry_id": "834fc100-c184-3b64-a6a1-565db79bf7ef",
                        "target_lang_word": "condor",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "condor",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "33cbd774-e654-3fda-8904-08925c9f8607",
                                        "entry_id": "ec0a9a2e-f494-35f2-9ed4-185e50f1098a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Non usuel désignant deux espèces d'oiseaux de la famille des Cathartidae : Gymnogyps californianus ou condor de Californie et principalement Vultur gryphus le condor des Andes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddd077ca-5859-4b0a-a3e4-a1e13a4dbc74",
                                                "sense_id": "33cbd774-e654-3fda-8904-08925c9f8607",
                                                "text": "Des oiseaux passaient à grand bruit d’ailes, et le moindre d’entre eux, par suite de cette illusion d’optique, paraissait plus grand qu’un condor ou un gypaète."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44c88915-2796-438b-9316-3aa34d6ceb81",
                                                "sense_id": "33cbd774-e654-3fda-8904-08925c9f8607",
                                                "text": "Des nuées de condors, de vautours et d’urubus vinrent tournoyer au-dessus des cadavres, sur lesquels ils s’abattirent en poussant des cris aigus et firent une horrible curée de chair humaine, …."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c961e2c9-9492-4bd4-a858-cc68244c5b9a",
                                                "sense_id": "33cbd774-e654-3fda-8904-08925c9f8607",
                                                "text": "Le condor andin, l’un des plus grands oiseaux du monde qui pèse de 9 à 15 kilos, est en danger critique d’extinction en Colombie et figure sur la liste rouge des espèces menacées de l’Union internationale pour la conservation de la nature (UICN) qui en dénombre 6.700 spécimens."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b194b5a-3bc1-39f3-a014-8257af7c3a71",
                                        "entry_id": "ec0a9a2e-f494-35f2-9ed4-185e50f1098a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Performance d’un joueur ou d’une joueuse qui réussit quatre coups sous le par."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Extrêmement rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "872ef2c0-65f1-34f0-952b-e7ee0e444578",
                                        "entry_id": "ec0a9a2e-f494-35f2-9ed4-185e50f1098a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ordre Bolivien de chevalerie."
                                        ],
